        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(release): preserve emoji in cross-OS response diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where cross-OS release diagnostics could contain malformed text when a fetched dashboard or Discord response placed an emoji across the response-body character limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe shared cross-OS response reader now reuses the repository's surrogate-safe truncation helper while preserving its existing cap, timeout behavior, stream cleanup, and `[truncated]` marker. Focused tests cover both split and complete surrogate-pair boundaries.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the dashboard and Discord callers, stream lifecycle, and shared helper contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCross-OS release checks keep fetched response text valid Unicode. Existing dashboard readiness checks, Discord requests, ASCII output, timeouts, and response-size policy are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: `\"abc\\u{1f600}tail\".slice(0, 4)` ends in lone UTF-16 code unit `0xd83d`.\n- A live read-only Discord API v10 request returned the documented JSON error shape with `message` and `code`. See https://docs.discord.com/developers/reference#error-messages.\n- Added focused coverage in `test/scripts/openclaw-cross-os-release-checks.test.ts` for split and complete surrogate-pair boundaries.\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check scripts/lib/cross-os-release-checks/network-smokes.ts test/scripts/openclaw-cross-os-release-checks.test.ts`\n- Exact-head CI run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29405007099: `check-lint` passed, `test/scripts/openclaw-cross-os-release-checks.test.ts` passed 104 tests in `checks-node-compact-small-4`, and `checks-windows-node-test` passed after validating the direct Node import on Windows.\n- The run's remaining failures are in untouched current-main surfaces: agent delegate test types, gateway method registration, state DB transaction isolation, and agent harness selection.\n",
